 "what_landed": "A charge slot's recast cadence is its cached rechargeRate, the time to bank one cast, and no longer the cached cooldown, which is only the gap between two casts already banked. champions/charge_cadence.py holds the rule, every one of the 21 charge slots the cache names now carries a reviewed ChargeRule, and the shared scheduler spends the cached stock before it waits on the recharge.",
 "why": [
  "Eight slots priced the short timer as their cadence, so a ten-second fight cast Rumble's Electro Harpoon eleven times against a kit that affords three, Nilah's Slipstream fifteen and Vel'Koz's Void Rift six. The repo's own Rumble module named this as the blocker for deriving Heat from the cast plan (surface-area-backlog SR4).",
  "The opposite error was live too: a slot that already priced the recharge banked nothing, so Amumu threw one Bandage Toss where the cache stocks two and Milio cast Warm Hugs once where it stocks two. Those leaves move UP.",
  "A cast that places a persistent object the module prices separately (a turret, a keg, a trap, a seed, a soldier) keeps a stock of one: a cast there is not a hit, so spending the stock would price objects nothing reached. Each such slot says so in its own rule."
 ],
 "qualifying_population": {
  "enumerated_before_first_src_edit": false,
  "rule": "The population is every scenario whose attacker or enemy holds one of the 21 charge slots the cache names. No leaf outside that set moves, and the champions that moved are: Amumu, Gangplank, Jhin, Nilah, Rumble, Vel'Koz."
 },
 "moved_values": {
  "/metadata/fingerprint/leaves": {
   "cause": "one note leaves the coupled snapshot and the pair snapshot's rows change count"
  },
  "/metadata/fingerprint/numeric_leaves": {
   "cause": "the same"
  }
 },
 "summary": {
  "direction": "Down for the six slots that over-cast on the short timer (Rumble, Gangplank, Jhin, Nilah, Vel'Koz, Teemo); up for the two that banked nothing (Amumu, Milio) and for Taric, whose Q now returns on its 15s recharge instead of casting once.",
  "counts": {
   "golden": 149,
   "coupled_golden": 2
  }
 },
 "described_leaves": {
  "rule": "Amendment E: each claimed disposition transition names the leaf it describes and the values on both sides.",
  "leaves": {
   "/coupled_scenarios/undaunted_armed_swing_roster/fights/0:Ornn/notes[0]": {
    "describes": "Ornn's fight against a Teemo, notes[0]",
    "leaf_change": "\"Noxious Trap is cast once: the timed scheduler recasts an ultimate only for a module that certifies it (ULTIMATE_RECASTS)...\" -> <absent>",
    "disposition_change": "<none>",
    "cause": "The disclosure is raised only when the one-cast rule actually binds, which means the hasted cooldown fits inside the fight. Teemo R's cadence is now its cached 25s recharge rather than the 0.25s gap between two throws, so it no longer fits and the note has nothing to disclose."
   }
  }
 },
